<!--
    Gilded Rift: spacing, focus and the shared ornament templates. Measurements: ../AGENTS.md, ../BRIEF.md and the two
    previews in ../art. Neither the League of Legends client nor Wild Rift publishes a spec, so the sizes come from the previews.
    Shared templates draw thin gold bevels, notched corners and diamonds. Sprites (Images/fx: rays.png, glow.png, spark.png)
    are white masks filled with theme brushes, so ThemeModifier edits reach them. Everything stretches; no template reports a
    wide desired size of its own (Statistics cards stay compact).

    CONTRACT. Every template below is a ControlTemplate for TargetType Control. Use it on a plain Control (or any Control
    subclass) as Template = DynamicResource of the key and read only the host properties listed here. All are
    IsHitTestVisible False. None has a content slot: the host overlays its own content in the same Grid cell (inside a margin
    of about half the cut where the plate is notched). Fixed pieces are 56px or less, the rest stretches to the host.
    Brushes are the host's Foreground unless the row names Background or BorderBrush. Where a row reads a theme brush
    directly it is a DynamicResource of that key, so ThemeModifier edits still apply.

    Key                    Reads                          Size behaviour                                  Example use
    DividerTemplate        Foreground                     Height 9; width free. 6px diamond at the left,  Rule between metadata groups, popup
                                                          1px rule from its centre fading to clear        separators. Foreground FrameBrush
    ChamferTemplate        Background, BorderBrush, Tag   Fills the host. Tag = cut size in px (double,   Play plate, chips, panels. Hosts keep
                                                          default 6); top-left and bottom-right cut,      their content in the same Grid cell
                                                          1px edge, corner cells are the Tag size
    BevelTemplate          Background, BevelLightBrush,   Fills the host. 1px lit top and left edges,     Raised plates
                           BevelShadowBrush               1px shadow bottom and right, faint inner line
    BevelInsetTemplate     Background, BevelLightBrush,   Fills the host. The inverse: shadow top and     Wells, inputs
                           BevelShadowBrush               left, lit bottom and right
    CornerMarksTemplate    Foreground                     Fills the host. 6px L-marks, 1.5px thick,       Cover hover (host animates its Margin
                                                          inset 2px from each corner                      3px inward), keyboard focus (FocusVisual)
    DoubleFrameTemplate    BorderBrush                    Fills the host. Outer 1px line (notch 6) and    Hovered or selected tile frame
                                                          an inner hairline inset 3px (notch 4) at 55%,
                                                          top-left and bottom-right corners notched
    BloomTemplate          Foreground                     Fills the host, no desired size. glow.png mask  Soft light behind a plate or glyph; host
                                                                                                          sets Opacity
    GlowFrameTemplate      Foreground                     Fills the host. Blurred stroked rectangle       Soft glow around a plate. Host sits at
                                                          inset 10px, bloom reaches about 8px outside     Margin -10 around it. Uses a BlurEffect
                                                          the plate                                       on one small rectangle, never on a row
    SelectionBarTemplate   Background (wash fading right  Fills the host. 3px bar at the left edge       Roster rows, tree rows, list items.
                           to clear at 85 percent),       with an 8px blurred copy, hairlines top and     The host's own content goes over it
                           BorderBrush (bar and glow),    bottom that fade to the right
                           Foreground (hairline sheen)
    TabItemIndicatorTemplate  Foreground                  Height 6; width free. 2px line fading to both   Under the selected tab header
                                                          ends and a soft light above it
    BrandMarkTemplate      Foreground                     Uniform scale to the host (natural 64x64).      Main menu crest, title band, empty page.
                                                          The winged gem of art/mark.svg, filled          Aspect is square; Background unused
    RingGlowTemplate       Foreground                     Fills the host. 1px ring plus a blurred copy,   Chosen slot or cover. Host sits at
                                                          ring inset 8px from the host edge               Margin -8 around the lit element
    GlowLineTemplate       Foreground                     Height 6; width free. Hot 1px core in           Light rule: running foot line, banner
                                                          HeadingForegroundBrush, 2px line, bloom         seam. Host sets Opacity
    WingsTemplate          Foreground (centre diamond     Height 40; width stretches (natural 360).       Settings title band, centred; the host
                           and outer feathers),           Three tapering feathers fan out of a 10x14      sets Width, desired width alone is about
                           BorderBrush (inner feathers)   diamond, mirrored                               240
    EmptyGameTemplate      Foreground (gold), BorderBrush Uniform scale to the host (natural 320x320).    The empty game page. Idle motion runs
                           (teal crystal light),          rays.png burst, glow.png core, faceted crystal  only while IsVisible; none of it goes
                           Background (plate behind the   that breathes (glow 0.7 to 1 over 4s), two     through a RenderTransform
                           rings)                         counter-marching dashed rings

    Details.
    ChamferTemplate: the cut cells are Path elements sized from Tag, so any size works and nothing is painted in a page colour.
    Tag may be written as plain text (Tag="8"); unset or not a number it falls back to 6. A host narrower than 2 x Tag squeezes the
    corner cells; keep plates at least 14px in each direction.
    PopupBorder is a plain Border style (PopupBackgroundBrush, 1px PopupBorderBrush, ControlCornerRadius). Popups and menus add the
    inner hairline themselves, the way ToolTip.xaml does: a child Border with Margin 1, BorderThickness 1 and BorderBrush
    FrameInnerBrush, so the hairline sits 2px in from the edge. Menu and list rows are 32px (MenuItemPadding, ComboBoxItemPadding).
    DoubleFrameTemplate and CornerMarksTemplate keep their cuts and arms at a fixed size, so a host below 16px squeezes them.
    GlowFrameTemplate and RingGlowTemplate draw outside the plate: the host needs a negative margin and a parent that does not
    clip. BlurEffect is used on small rectangles only, never on the host that holds text.
    WingsTemplate: columns are 62 star, 104 star, 28, 104 star, 62 star so that the natural 360px host keeps the previews' proportions.
    EmptyGameTemplate: the 480 unit rays sit in a Canvas so WPF's layout clip does not cut them to the 320 stage.
    The dashed rings turn by animating StrokeDashOffset (a dash pattern marching round the circle) and the
    breath animates Opacity, so no transform is animated. The ring diameters make the circumference a whole number of dash
    periods: do not change a diameter without changing its dash array.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <Style x:Key="PopupBorder" TargetType="Border">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource PopupBackgroundBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource PopupBorderBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="{DynamicResource PopupBorderThickness}" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{DynamicResource ControlCornerRadius}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Spacing. Buttons: a 12px semibold label with a 20px inset on a 32px plate (the preview's .btn). Inputs: 10px inset.
         Menu and list rows are 32px (14px of text and 7px above and below); the left inset leaves room for the 2-3px gold bar. -->
    <Thickness x:Key="ButtonPadding">20,5</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="InputPadding">10,5</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="MenuPadding">4</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="MenuItemPadding">14,7</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="ComboBoxDropDownPadding">4</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="ComboBoxItemPadding">14,7</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="ListBoxItemPadding">14,6</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="GroupBoxPadding">16,12,16,14</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="GroupBoxHeaderMargin">0,0,0,8</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="TooltipPadding">10,5</Thickness>
    <!-- Every form field and button: one height across all themes (validate-extension.ps1, FormControlHeight). -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="ControlHeight">32</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="IconSize">16</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="GameBannerHeight">300</sys:Double>
    <!-- Banner darkening (ThemeModifier slider, 0 = none; above 0 the tint is 50% + 50% x the value): GameBannerTintBrush over the banner art, under the
         theme's own fade. Off while Playnite draws the art behind the window (the banner collapses then). -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="GameBannerDarken">0</sys:Double>

    <!-- Keyboard focus: the four gold-white corner marks of the champion grid, one pixel outside the control. -->
    <Style x:Key="FocusVisual" TargetType="Control">
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Control Template="{DynamicResource CornerMarksTemplate}" Foreground="{DynamicResource FocusBrush}" Margin="-3" Focusable="False" IsHitTestVisible="False" />
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

    <!-- ===== shared ornament templates ===== -->

    <!-- Divider: a 6px diamond with a 1px rule running right from its centre, fading to clear. Height 9. Foreground. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="DividerTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid Height="9" IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="3,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M3,0 L6,3 L3,6 L0,3 Z" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Plate with the top-left and bottom-right corners cut by Tag px (default 6). Background = the body, BorderBrush = the 1px edge.
         A 3x3 grid whose corner cells are the Tag size: rectangles for the body, borders for the sides, a triangle and a diagonal
         stroke per cut, so it fits any size and paints nothing in a page colour. The host overlays its content in the same cell. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="ChamferTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid SnapsToDevicePixels="True" UseLayoutRounding="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
                <RowDefinition Height="*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <Path Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Stretch="Fill" Data="M1,0 L1,1 L0,1 Z" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                  Width="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}"
                  Height="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}" />
            <Path Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="2" Stretch="Fill" Data="M0,0 L1,0 L0,1 Z" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                  Width="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}"
                  Height="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}" />
            <Rectangle Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
            <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
            <Rectangle Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
            <Border Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
            <Border Grid.Row="0" Grid.RowSpan="2" Grid.Column="2" BorderThickness="0,0,1,0" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
            <Border Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
            <Border Grid.Row="1" Grid.RowSpan="2" Grid.Column="0" BorderThickness="1,0,0,0" BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
            <Path Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Stretch="Fill" Data="M0,1 L1,0" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1"
                  Width="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}"
                  Height="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}" />
            <Path Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="2" Stretch="Fill" Data="M1,0 L0,1" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1"
                  Width="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}"
                  Height="{Binding Tag, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, FallbackValue=6, TargetNullValue=6}" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Raised plate: Background body, a lit 1px edge top and left (BevelLightBrush), a shadow edge bottom and right (BevelShadowBrush),
         and a fainter inner line on each pair so the plate reads as bevelled and not just outlined. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="BevelTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid SnapsToDevicePixels="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="1,1,1,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="1,1,0,1" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="1,0,1,1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,1,1,1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Sunken plate (wells): the inverse of BevelTemplate. Shadow top and left, lit bottom and right. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="BevelInsetTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid SnapsToDevicePixels="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="1,1,1,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="1,1,0,1" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="1,0,1,1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,1,1,1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" Opacity="0.3" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelLightBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" />
            <Rectangle Width="1" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{DynamicResource BevelShadowBrush}" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Corner marks: four L shapes, arm 6, 1.5px thick, inset 2px from the host's corners. Foreground. Hosts animate their Margin
         for the cover hover (the marks tighten 3px inward); FocusVisual puts them 3px outside the control. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="CornerMarksTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid Margin="2" SnapsToDevicePixels="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M0,6 L0,0 L6,0 L6,1.5 L1.5,1.5 L1.5,6 Z" />
            <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M0,0 L6,0 L6,6 L4.5,6 L4.5,1.5 L0,1.5 Z" />
            <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M0,0 L1.5,0 L1.5,4.5 L6,4.5 L6,6 L0,6 Z" />
            <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M4.5,0 L6,0 L6,6 L0,6 L0,4.5 L4.5,4.5 Z" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Double frame: an outer 1px line with the top-left and bottom-right corners cut 6px, and an inner hairline inset 3px
         with its own cut of 4px (parallel to the outer diagonal) at 55%. BorderBrush draws both. No fill. Each frame is edge
         rectangles that stop short of the cuts plus a diagonal stroke per cut. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="DoubleFrameTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid SnapsToDevicePixels="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Grid>
                <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="6,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,0,0,6" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="0,0,6,0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,6,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" Data="M0,6.5 L6.5,0" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                <Path Width="6" Height="6" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Data="M-0.5,6 L6,-0.5" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
            </Grid>
            <Grid Margin="3" Opacity="0.55">
                <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="4,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,0,0,4" HorizontalAlignment="Right" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Height="1" Margin="0,0,4,0" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Rectangle Width="1" Margin="0,4,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
                <Path Width="4" Height="4" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top" Data="M0,4.5 L4.5,0" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                <Path Width="4" Height="4" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Data="M-0.5,4 L4,-0.5" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
            </Grid>
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Bloom: the white glow.png mask stretched over the host and filled with Foreground. No desired size. The host sets Opacity. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="BloomTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                <ImageBrush ImageSource="{ThemeFile 'Images/fx/glow.png'}" Stretch="Fill" />
            </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
        </Rectangle>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Glow frame: a 3px stroked rectangle inset 10px from the host, blurred 8px, so the light reaches about 8px outside the plate it
         lights. The host sits at Margin -10 around that plate and may set Opacity. Foreground. The blur is on this one rectangle only. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="GlowFrameTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Rectangle Margin="10" Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="3" RadiusX="3" RadiusY="3">
                <Rectangle.Effect>
                    <BlurEffect Radius="8" />
                </Rectangle.Effect>
            </Rectangle>
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- The selection plate (roster rows, tree rows, list items): a wash from Background that is full at the left edge and clear by 85 percent of
         the width, hairlines of Foreground along the top and bottom that fade to the right, and a 3px bar of BorderBrush at the left edge with a
         blurred copy of the bar beside it (the glow is the copy, not an effect on the row). Fills the host. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="SelectionBarTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid SnapsToDevicePixels="True" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.85" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.5">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.5">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Width="3" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" Opacity="0.75">
                <Rectangle.Effect>
                    <BlurEffect Radius="8" />
                </Rectangle.Effect>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Width="3" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Tab indicator under the selected header: a 2px line of Foreground that fades out toward both ends, with a soft light rising above it
         (a radial mask centred on the foot). Height 6, the width follows the host. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="TabItemIndicatorTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid Height="6" IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.35">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <RadialGradientBrush Center="0.5,1" GradientOrigin="0.5,1" RadiusX="0.5" RadiusY="1">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1" />
                    </RadialGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Height="2" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0.2" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0.8" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- The brand mark on a 64 unit square: a diamond centre stone (two narrow facets over a long point), three swept feathers on each side
         and a small base chevron. Same geometry as art/mark.svg, filled in the host Foreground. Square aspect. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="BrandMarkTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Viewbox Stretch="Uniform" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Canvas Width="64" Height="64">
                <Path Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                      Data="M31,7 L23,20 L31,50 Z M33,7 L41,20 L33,50 Z M22,23 L2,14 L9,25 Z M22,28 L4,26 L11,34 Z M23,33 L8,38 L15,44 Z M42,23 L62,14 L55,25 Z M42,28 L60,26 L53,34 Z M41,33 L56,38 L49,44 Z M32,54 L36.5,57.5 L32,61 L27.5,57.5 Z" />
            </Canvas>
        </Viewbox>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Ring glow: a 1px ring inset 8px from the host and a blurred 3px copy of it, in Foreground. The host sits at Margin -8 around the
         element it marks, so the ring runs along that element's edge and the bloom reaches about 6px past it. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="RingGlowTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Rectangle Margin="8" Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="3" RadiusX="2" RadiusY="2" Opacity="0.7">
                <Rectangle.Effect>
                    <BlurEffect Radius="6" />
                </Rectangle.Effect>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Margin="8" Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1" RadiusX="2" RadiusY="2" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Light line, 6px tall: a bloom (radial mask over the whole strip), a 2px line and a 1px hot core in HeadingForegroundBrush, all fading
         at the ends. Foreground draws the bloom and the line. No desired width. The host may set Opacity. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="GlowLineTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid Height="6" IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Rectangle Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.35">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <RadialGradientBrush Center="0.5,0.5" GradientOrigin="0.5,0.5" RadiusX="0.5" RadiusY="0.5">
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1" />
                    </RadialGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Height="2" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.85">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0.12" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0.88" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="1" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
            <Rectangle Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{DynamicResource HeadingForegroundBrush}" Opacity="0.9">
                <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    <LinearGradientBrush StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.1" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Black" Offset="0.5" />
                        <GradientStop Color="Transparent" Offset="0.9" />
                    </LinearGradientBrush>
                </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
            </Rectangle>
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- Wings: three tapering feathers fanning out of a centre diamond, mirrored. 40px tall, the width stretches (natural 360). Columns
         62*, 104*, 28, 104*, 62* keep the preview's proportions at 360. A wing is a 104x22 drawing in a Viewbox stretched sideways only
         (the drawing starts 10px down, so the diamond sits on the 21px centre line). Foreground = outer feather and diamond,
         BorderBrush = the two inner feathers. The right wing is the left one flipped. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="WingsTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Grid Height="40" IsHitTestVisible="False" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="62*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="104*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="28" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="104*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="62*" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Viewbox Grid.Column="1" Stretch="Fill" Height="22" Margin="0,10,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <Canvas Width="104" Height="22">
                    <Path Data="M104,11 C78,11 50,6 0,0" Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1.2" />
                    <Path Data="M104,14 C80,15 54,15 14,11" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                    <Path Data="M104,17 C84,19 64,22 36,22" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                </Canvas>
            </Viewbox>
            <Viewbox Grid.Column="3" Stretch="Fill" Height="22" Margin="0,10,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                <Viewbox.RenderTransform>
                    <ScaleTransform ScaleX="-1" ScaleY="1" />
                </Viewbox.RenderTransform>
                <Canvas Width="104" Height="22">
                    <Path Data="M104,11 C78,11 50,6 0,0" Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1.2" />
                    <Path Data="M104,14 C80,15 54,15 14,11" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                    <Path Data="M104,17 C84,19 64,22 36,22" Stroke="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                </Canvas>
            </Viewbox>
            <Path Grid.Column="2" Width="10" Height="14" Margin="0,14,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Data="M5,0 L10,7 L5,14 L0,7 Z" />
        </Grid>
    </ControlTemplate>

    <!-- The empty game page: a 320 unit stage. Back to front: the rays.png burst (Foreground, 480 units so it spreads past the stage), a
         Background plate disc, the glow.png core (BorderBrush, the crystal's light), two dashed rings marching in opposite directions
         (Foreground), and a faceted gem (facets BorderBrush, edges Foreground, a lit facet in HeadingForegroundBrush). The glow and the gem breathe
         between 0.7 and 1 over 4 seconds, the rings march one whole turn per 60 and 45 seconds. Everything runs from a Trigger on IsVisible
         in the template, so nothing runs while the page is hidden, and nothing goes through a RenderTransform. -->
    <ControlTemplate x:Key="EmptyGameTemplate" TargetType="Control">
        <Viewbox Stretch="Uniform" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <Grid Width="320" Height="320" SnapsToDevicePixels="True">
                <Canvas IsHitTestVisible="False">
                    <Rectangle Canvas.Left="-80" Canvas.Top="-80" Width="480" Height="480" Fill="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" Opacity="0.3">
                        <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                            <ImageBrush ImageSource="{ThemeFile 'Images/fx/rays.png'}" Stretch="Uniform" />
                        </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                    </Rectangle>
                </Canvas>
                <Ellipse Width="200" Height="200" Fill="{TemplateBinding Background}" />
                <Rectangle x:Name="CoreGlow" Width="300" Height="300" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" Opacity="0.85">
                    <Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                        <ImageBrush ImageSource="{ThemeFile 'Images/fx/glow.png'}" Stretch="Uniform" />
                    </Rectangle.OpacityMask>
                </Rectangle>
                <Ellipse x:Name="RingA" Width="254.6479" Height="254.6479" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1" StrokeDashArray="2 6" Opacity="0.6" />
                <Ellipse x:Name="RingB" Width="210.0845" Height="210.0845" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                         Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1" StrokeDashArray="10 5 2 5" Opacity="0.8" />
                <Canvas x:Name="Crystal" Width="320" Height="320" Opacity="0.85">
                    <Path Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" Opacity="0.5" Data="M160,92 L130,152 L160,232 Z" />
                    <Path Fill="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}" Opacity="0.9" Data="M160,92 L190,152 L160,232 Z" />
                    <Path Fill="{DynamicResource HeadingForegroundBrush}" Opacity="0.35" Data="M160,92 L145,152 L160,152 Z" />
                    <Path Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1" Opacity="0.8" Data="M130,152 L190,152 M160,92 L160,232" />
                    <Path Stroke="{TemplateBinding Foreground}" StrokeThickness="1.6" StrokeLineJoin="Miter" Data="M160,92 L190,152 L160,232 L130,152 Z" />
                    <Path Fill="{DynamicResource HeadingForegroundBrush}" Opacity="0.85" Data="M160,126 L166,144 L160,162 L154,144 Z" />
                </Canvas>
            </Grid>
        </Viewbox>
        <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
            <Trigger Property="IsVisible" Value="True">
                <Trigger.EnterActions>
                    <BeginStoryboard x:Name="EmptyGameIdle">
                        <Storyboard>
                            <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="CoreGlow" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity" From="0.7" To="1" Duration="0:0:2" AutoReverse="True" RepeatBehavior="Forever">
                                <DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                                    <CubicEase EasingMode="EaseInOut" />
                                </DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                            </DoubleAnimation>
                            <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="Crystal" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity" From="0.7" To="1" Duration="0:0:2" AutoReverse="True" RepeatBehavior="Forever">
                                <DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                                    <CubicEase EasingMode="EaseInOut" />
                                </DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                            </DoubleAnimation>
                            <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="RingA" Storyboard.TargetProperty="StrokeDashOffset" From="0" To="96" Duration="0:1:0" RepeatBehavior="Forever" />
                            <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="RingB" Storyboard.TargetProperty="StrokeDashOffset" From="0" To="-66" Duration="0:0:45" RepeatBehavior="Forever" />
                        </Storyboard>
                    </BeginStoryboard>
                </Trigger.EnterActions>
                <Trigger.ExitActions>
                    <RemoveStoryboard BeginStoryboardName="EmptyGameIdle" />
                </Trigger.ExitActions>
            </Trigger>
        </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
    </ControlTemplate>
</ResourceDictionary>
